From 86b32af49de83a0484dd5e9136c7794114182ebc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 14:35:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Hades][Network] Projector control: the anamorphic mode of a
 JVC by the shape of the picture

An owner of a JVC NZ800 asked for JVC's anamorphic modes next to the
lens memories: with an anamorphic lens the projector has to be told
Off, A, B, C or D for each shape of picture, and a lens memory alone
does not cover a lens that stays in place without memories.

JVC's External Command Communication Specification has the command:
INVS, "Anamorphic switch", with "0" Off, "1" A, "2" B, "3" C and "4" D
(NZ800/NZ900, Ver. 2.0 of 8 Oct 2025, table 4-58; NZ500/NZ700, Ver. 1.0
of 6 Nov 2024). The models of 2018 have A to C, those of 2015 A and B.
A projector ignores a value it does not have: the command then gets no
acknowledgement, which the control already takes as refused and does
not send again.

Each class of shape (narrower, wide, widest) now has, on a JVC, an
anamorphic mode of its own, "Leave it as it is" by default: nothing
changes for anyone who does not set one. It follows the shape with the
lens memory, with the same hold and band, and goes back with "Back to
the memory for narrower pictures when the video ends". It is sent
after the lens memory, in the same talk: a JVC's installation mode
holds an anamorphic mode of its own (the NZ800's manual: "Installation
Mode... Lens Control, Pixel Adjust, Mask, Anamorphic..."), so a memory
recalled after it would undo it; a memory recalled marks the anamorphic
mode as unknown, and the one of the class is sent again.

So that an anamorphic lens without lens memories can be followed, the
lens memory for narrower and for wide pictures may now be None (the
lens is not moved for them), as the widest already could; the widest
pictures are a class of their own where a memory or an anamorphic mode
is set for them.

Sony and Epson: Hades has no command of theirs for it from an official
reference (their aspect modes for an anamorphic lens are menu settings
in their manuals), so the settings show only for JVC.

The test of the connection is waited for one command longer
(TestWaitMs()), the player information names the anamorphic mode sent,
and the strings are in English and in the three Spanish languages of
Estuary.
